1
00:00:02,874 --> 00:00:05,374
(Bert:)Thank you very much.
Thanks.

2
00:00:05,376 --> 00:00:06,476
(Leonard:)That is unbelievable.

3
00:00:06,478 --> 00:00:07,708
(Leonard:)Good for Bert.

4
00:00:07,712 --> 00:00:10,212
(Howard:)Damn, the MacArthur
Genius Grant.

5
00:00:10,215 --> 00:00:11,715
(Raj:)Couldn't have happened
to a nicer guy.

6
00:00:11,716 --> 00:00:14,486
(Sheldon:)Everything is stupid
and I want to go home.

7
00:00:15,487 --> 00:00:17,387
(Leonard:)That's Sheldon's way of saying

8
00:00:17,388 --> 00:00:18,618
(Leonard:)he's proud of Bert, too.

9
00:00:18,623 --> 00:00:19,893
(Howard:)Ah.

10
00:00:19,891 --> 00:00:21,821
(Sheldon:)Hey, it's not even called
the "Genius Grant,"

11
00:00:21,826 --> 00:00:23,626
(Sheldon:)it's the MacArthur Fellowship.

12
00:00:23,628 --> 00:00:25,758
(Sheldon:)Just like it's
not Frankenstein,

13
00:00:25,763 --> 00:00:26,963
it's "Frankenstein's Monster."

14
00:00:26,965 --> 00:00:27,935
(Sheldon:)Which brings us back

15
00:00:27,932 --> 00:00:29,932
(Sheldon:)to that hulking
simpleton over there.

16
00:00:31,803 --> 00:00:33,073
(Sheldon:)And if anyone's a genius,

17
00:00:33,071 --> 00:00:34,941
(Sheldon:)it's me for the way
I brought that full circle.

18
00:00:36,875 --> 00:00:38,105
(Leonard:)How much money did he win?

19
00:00:38,109 --> 00:00:39,339
(Raj:)Over half a million dollars.

20
00:00:39,344 --> 00:00:40,844
(Penny:)- Wow.
- And he doesn't have to use it

21
00:00:40,845 --> 00:00:43,145
(Howard:)for research, he can do
whatever he wants with it.

22
00:00:43,148 --> 00:00:46,648
(Sheldon:)Oh, good, maybe he can build
a nicer bridge to live under.

23
00:00:47,585 --> 00:00:49,155
(Howard:)Here he comes.
Right.

24
00:00:49,154 --> 00:00:50,124
(Leonard:)Be polite.

25
00:00:50,121 --> 00:00:51,321
(Sheldon:)I know how to behave.

26
00:00:51,322 --> 00:00:52,592
(Howard:)Do you?

27
00:00:52,590 --> 00:00:54,590
(Sheldon:)Hey,
congratulations Bert!

28
00:00:54,592 --> 00:00:55,792
(Leonard:)Yeah, good for you.
That's amazing.

29
00:00:55,793 --> 00:00:56,763
(Bert:)Thanks.

30
00:00:56,761 --> 00:00:58,791
(Bert:)I was as surprised as anybody.

31
00:00:58,796 --> 00:00:59,796
(Bert:)When they called
and told me

32
00:00:59,797 --> 00:01:01,267
(Bert:)I won, I didn't believe them.

33
00:01:01,266 --> 00:01:03,396
(Bert:)And then they said,
"No, you really won."

34
00:01:03,401 --> 00:01:06,331
And then I said, "Cool."

35
00:01:06,337 --> 00:01:08,837
(Sheldon:)Someone call
George R. R. Martin,

36
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:11,140
(Sheldon:)this guy knows how
to finish a story.

37
00:01:11,142 --> 00:01:14,382
(Bert:)I've gotten pretty good
at telling it.

38
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:17,010
(Bert:)Well, see ya.

39
00:01:18,082 --> 00:01:19,452
(Sheldon:)Some genius.

40
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:22,390
(Sheldon:)I zinged him with sarcasm,
he didn't even notice.

41
00:01:23,254 --> 00:01:24,484
(Leonard:)I know, and it was

42
00:01:24,489 --> 00:01:26,659
(Leonard:)the greatest sarcastic
quip I've ever heard.

43
00:01:26,658 --> 00:01:29,858
(Sheldon:)Well, aren't you a peach.

44
00:01:29,861 --> 00:01:33,501
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

